The correct answer is f(x) = a₀(x² + c)ⁿ with a₀ > 0 and c > 0, so all roots equal ±i√c. This follows from AM-GM giving Σ eⱼeₙ₋ⱼ ≥ C(2n,n)eₙ, with equality forcing all bᵢ equal.

The submitted answer says f(x) = a₀∏(x² + bᵢ²) with arbitrary positive bᵢ, which allows unequal bᵢ. Its derivation is also flawed (e.g., spurious factors of 2 in the Vieta expressions). Counterexample: n=2, bᵢ² = 1 and 4 gives lhs 33 > rhs 24, so condition (2) fails. The submitted family is therefore too large and incorrect.

{"pass": false, "reason": "Condition (2) forces all b_i equal, so f = a0(x^2+c)^n; the submitted answer allows arbitrary distinct b_i, which fails (e.g. n=2, b^2=1,4 gives 33 > 24)."}

